  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The analysis is a qualitative case study of a single city under a specific municipal administration, which may limit its direct application to cities with different governance structures or housing market dynamics.",
      "what": "This study analyzes Barcelona's municipal policies between 2015 and 2023, examining how the local government attempted to coordinate sustainable mobility initiatives, specifically the superblock experiments, with housing policies designed to curb gentrification and increase public housing supply.",
      "why": "It documents a concrete policy attempt to resolve the tension between urban greening and housing displacement, showing how mobility and housing strategies can be intentionally integrated to protect vulnerable residents from the inflationary effects of public space improvements."
    }
